          %h3#relation_to_cartan_model_for_equivariant_de_rham_cohomology Relation to Cartan model for equivariant de Rham cohomology
          %p
            The Weil algebra may be identified with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartan+model"} Cartan model
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+de+Rham+cohomology"} equivariant de Rham cohomology
            for the special case of the Lie group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            acting on itself by right multiplication. Concersely, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartan+models"} Cartan models
            form a generalization of the Weil algebra. See at
            %em
              %a{:href => "equivariant+de+Rham+cohomology#TheCartanModel"} equivariant de Rham cohomology – Cartan model
            for more.
          %h2#AsInnerDer
            As the CE-algebra of the
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
          %p
            By the discussion at
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Lie+algebra"} ∞-Lie algebra
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebra"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra
            %em identify
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} opposite category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dgAlg"} dgAlg
            on commutative
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semi-free+dga"} semi-free dga
            = succeed "s/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Lie+algebra"} ∞-Lie algebra
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Lie+algebroid"} ∞-Lie algebroid
          %p
            That means that the Weil algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(\mathfrak{g})
            of some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebra"} L-∞ algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            is the Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra of
            %em another
            = succeed "-Lie" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              For any
              = succeed "-Lie" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
              write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi inn
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} inn(\mathfrak{g})
              for the
              = succeed "-Lie" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(\mathfrak{g})
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CE
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi inn
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    CE(inn(\mathfrak{g}))
                    \\coloneqq
                    W(\mathfrak{g})
                    \\,.
          %p
            In the following we discuss these
            %em
              inner automorphism
              = succeed "-Lie" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            in more detail. (See section 6 of (
            %a{:href => "#SSSI"}> SSSI
            )).
          %h3#for_an_ordinary_lie_algebra For an ordinary Lie algebra
          .num_lemma
            %h6#observation_2 Observation
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
              an ordinary
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inner+derivation+Lie+2-algebra"} inner derivation Lie 2-algebra
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+Lie+2-algebra"} strict Lie 2-algebra
              given by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-Lie+algebra"} dg-Lie algebra
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi inn
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi d
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    inn(\mathfrak{g}) = ( \mathfrak{g} \stackrel{d}{\to} \mathfrak{g}, [-,-])
            %p whose
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  elements in degree -1 are the elements
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi x
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi 𝔤
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in \mathfrak{g}
                  = succeed "s" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivation"} derivation
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ι
                          %mi x
                        %mo :
                        %mi CE
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi 𝔤
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %mi CE
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi 𝔤
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \iota_x : CE(\mathfrak{g}) \to CE(\mathfrak{g})
                %p
                  given by contraction with
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi x
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              %li
                %p elements in degree 0 are the derivations of degree 0 that are of the form
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ℒ
                          %mi X
                        %mo ≔
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msub
                          %mi d
                          %mrow
                            %mi CE
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi 𝔤
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi ι
                          %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi CE
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi 𝔤
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %mi CE
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi 𝔤
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\mathcal{L}_X
                        \\coloneqq
                        [d_{CE(\mathfrak{g})}, \iota_x]
                        \\colon
                        CE(\mathfrak{g}) \to CE(\mathfrak{g})
                  ;
              %li
                %p
                  the differential
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msub
                          %mi d
                          %mi CE
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo :
                        %mi 𝔤
                        %mo →
                        %mi 𝔤
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d = [d_{CE}, -] : \mathfrak{g} \to \mathfrak{g}
                  is the commutator of derivations with the differential
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi d
                            %mrow
                              %mi CE
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi 𝔤
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_{CE(\mathfrak{g})}
              %li
                %p the bracket is the graded commutator of derivations.
          %p
            Equivalently this is identified with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+crossed+module"} differential crossed module
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi Id
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathfrak{g} \stackrel{Id}{\to} \mathfrak{g})
            with the action being the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+action"} adjoint action
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            on itself.
          %p
            One checks that for all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x, y \in \mathfrak{g}
            we have in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi inn
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} inn(\mathfrak{g})
            the brackets
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msub
                        %mi ι
                        %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi ι
                        %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\iota_x, \iota_y] = 0
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msub
                        %mi ℒ
                        %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi ι
                        %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi ι
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi x
                          %mo ,
                          %mi y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\mathcal{L}_x, \iota_y] = \iota_{[x,y]}
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msub
                        %mi ℒ
                        %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi ℒ
                        %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi ℒ
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi x
                          %mo ,
                          %mi y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\mathcal{L}_x, \mathcal{L}_y] = \mathcal{L}_{[x,y]}
          %p and of course
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ℒ
                      %mi x
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi d
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi ι
                      %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}_x = [d, \iota_x]
              \.
          %p
            These identities are known as
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartan+calculus"} Cartan calculus
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℒ
                    %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}_x
            is called a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+derivative"} Lie derivative
          %p
            In this sense one may understand
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi inn
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} inn(\mathfrak{g})
            for general
            = succeed "-Lie" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            as providing an
            = succeed "-version" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartan+calculus"} Cartan calculus
          %h2#relation_to_other_concepts Relation to other concepts
          %h3#LieAlgValuedForms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            \-Lie algebra valued differential forms
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Lie+algebra"} ∞-Lie algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Lie+algebra+valued+differential+form"} ∞-Lie algebra valued differential form
            is a morphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ←
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Omega^\bullet(X) \leftarrow W(\mathfrak{g}) : A
          %p
            of
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-algebra"} dg-algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+complex"} de Rham complex
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            The image of the unshifted generators
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mo ∧
                    %mn 1
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo *
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A : \wedge^1 \mathfrak{g}^* \to \Omega^\bullet(X)
            are the forms themselves, the image of the shifted generators
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mi A
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mo ∧
                    %mn 1
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_A : \wedge^1 \mathfrak{g}^*[1]
            are the corresponding
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curvature"} curvature
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bianchi+identity"} Bianchi identity
            on the curvatures.
          %p
            Precisely if the curvatures vanish does the morphism factor through the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebra"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi CE
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(\mathfrak{g}) \to CE(\mathfrak{g})
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mi A
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ⇔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi CE
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi 𝔤
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∃
                                  %msub
                                    %mi A
                                    %mi flat
                            %mo ↙
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi Ω
                              %mo •
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ←
                              %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mi W
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi 𝔤
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (F_A = 0)
                  \\;\;\Leftrightarrow
                  \\;\;
                  \\left(
                  \\array{
                  \&amp;&amp; CE(\mathfrak{g})
                  \\\
                  \&amp; {}^{\mathllap{\exists A_{flat}}}\swarrow &amp; \uparrow
                  \\\
                  \\Omega^\bullet(X) &amp;\stackrel{A}{\leftarrow}&amp; W(\mathfrak{g})
                  }
                  \\right)
                  \\,.
          %h3#invariant_polynomials_and_chernsimons_elements Invariant polynomials and Chern-Simons elements
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycle"} cocycle
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Lie+algebra+cohomology"} ∞-Lie algebra cohomology
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Lie+algebra"} ∞-Lie algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            is a closed element in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebra"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CE
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CE(\mathfrak{g})
          %p
            An
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariant+polynomial"} invariant polynomial
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle -\rangle
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            is a closed element in the Weil algebra
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle -\rangle \in W(\mathfrak{g})
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mo ∧
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle - \rangle \in \wedge^\bullet (\mathfrak{g}^*[1])
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mo ∧
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\langle -\rangle  \in \wedge^\bullet( \mathfrak{g}^*[1] )
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  d_{W(\mathfrak{g})} \langle -\rangle = 0
                  \\,.
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in \mathfrak{g}
            an element of the
            = succeed "-Lie" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ι
                    %mi x
                  %mo :
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\iota_x : W(\mathfrak{g}) \to W(\mathfrak{g})
          %p
            the evident operation of contraction with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ι
                    %mi x
                  %mo :
                  %mi t
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\iota_x : t \mapsto t(x)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ι
                    %mi x
                  %mo :
                  %mi σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↦
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\iota_x : \sigma(t) \mapsto 0
          %p
            extended as a graded derivation. Then the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+derivative"} Lie derivative
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℒ
                    %mi x
                  %mo ≔
                  %msub
                    %mi ad
                    %mi x
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi ι
                    %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathcal{L}_x
                  \\coloneqq ad_x
                  \\coloneqq
                  [d_{W(\mathfrak{g})}, \iota_x]
                  \\colon
                  W(\mathfrak{g}) \to W(\mathfrak{g})
          %p
            encodes the coadjoint action of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}^*
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariant+polynomial"} invariant polynomial
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle - \rangle
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ι
                    %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\iota_x \langle - \rangle = 0
          %p and
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  d_{W(\mathfrak{g})} \langle - \rangle = 0
          %p and hence
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ad
                    %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  ad_x \langle -\rangle  = 0
                  \\,.
          %p
            Since the cohomology of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(\mathfrak{g})
            is trivial, there is necessarily for each invariant polynomial an element
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi cs
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cs_{\langle -\rangle}
            such that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mi cs
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  d_{W(\mathfrak{g})} cs_{\langle -\rangle} =
                  \\langle -\rangle
                  \\,.
          %p
            This is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+element"} Chern-Simons element
            of the invariant polynomial. Notice, crucially, that this is ingeneral
            %em not
            restricted to the shifted part
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mo ∧
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \wedge^\bullet (\mathfrak{g}^*[1])
            Its restriction
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi μ
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mo ≔
                  %msub
                    %mi cs
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mo ∧
                        %mo •
                      %msup
                        %mi 𝔤
                        %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mu_{\langle -\rangle}
                  \\coloneqq
                  cs_{\langle - \rangle}|_{\wedge^\bullet \mathfrak{g}^*}
          %p
            to the unshifted copy, hence to the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebra"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle - \rangle
          %p For
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (A,F_A) \colon W(\mathfrak{g}) \to \Omega^\bullet(X)
          %p
            a collection of
            = succeed "-valued" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "LieAlgValuedForms"} above
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mo :
                  %mi CE
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi b
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle -\rangle  : CE(b^{n-1}\mathbb{R}) \to W(\mathfrak{g})
            an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariant+polynomial"} invariant polynomial
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mo :
                  %mi CE
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi b
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi F
                        %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\langle F_A\rangle
                  \:
                  CE(b^{n-1}\mathbb{R})
                  \\stackrel{\langle - \rangle}{\to}
                  W(\mathfrak{g})
                  \\stackrel{(A,F_A)}{\to}
                  \\Omega^\bullet(X)
          %p
            is the corresponding
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curvature+characteristic+form"} curvature characteristic form
            = succeed "-form" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mo ,
                  %mi cs
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi b
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\langle - \rangle, cs) : W(b^{n-1}) \to W(\mathfrak{g})
            the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+element"} Chern-Simons element
            we have that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi cs
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cs(A,F_A)
            is the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+form"} Chern-Simons form
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#WeilofLieAlg Weil algebra of a Lie algebra
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            be a finite dimensional
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebroid"} Lie algebroid
            has as base manifold the point,
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 0
                    %mo =
                    %mi pt
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_0 = pt
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mo ∧
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo •
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \wedge^\bullet_{C^\infty(X_0)} \mathfrak{g}^*
            is just a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grassmann+algebra"} Grassmann algebra
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebra"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra
            is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi CE
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mo ∧
                    %mo •
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo *
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  CE(\mathfrak{g}) = (\wedge^\bullet \mathfrak{g}^*, d_{\mathfrak{g}})
                  \\,,
          %p
            where the differential acts on the elements of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}^*
            in degree 1 by the linear dual of the Lie bracket.
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi 𝔤
                        %mo *
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo *
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo *
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo *
                  %mo ∧
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo *
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  d \mathfrak{g}|_{\mathfrak{g}^*} = [-,-]^* : \mathfrak{g}^* \to \mathfrak{g}^* \wedge \mathfrak{g}^*
                  \\,.
          %p
            The corresponding Weil algebra is obtained by adding another copy of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}^*
            in degree 2
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mo ∧
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo *
                  %mo ⊕
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  W(\mathfrak{g}) = (\wedge^\bullet (\mathfrak{g}^* \oplus \mathfrak{g}^*[1]), d_{W(\mathfrak{g})})
          %p
            where with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi σ
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo *
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma : \mathfrak{g}^* \to \mathfrak{g}^*[1]
            the degree shift isomorphism, the differential acts as
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi 𝔤
                        %mo *
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                  %mi σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  d_{W(\mathfrak{g})}|_{\mathfrak{g}^*}
                  \:
                  [-,-]^* + \sigma
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi 𝔤
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo :
                  %mi σ
                  %mo ∘
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mrow
                      %mi CE
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∘
                  %msup
                    %mi σ
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  d_{W(\mathfrak{g})}|_{\mathfrak{g}^*[1]}
                  \:
                  \\sigma \circ d_{CE(\mathfrak{g})} \circ \sigma^{-1}
                  \\,.
          %p For illustration, we spell this out in a basis.
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi t
                    %mi a
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{t_a\}_a
            be a basis for the underlying vector space of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            and let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi a
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{C^a{}_{b c}\}
            be the corresponding structure constants of the Lie bracket
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi t
                    %mi b
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi t
                    %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi a
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mi c
                  %msub
                    %mi t
                    %mi a
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  [t_b, t_c] = C^a{}_{b c} t_a
                  \\,.
          %p
            Then the Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra is generated on generators
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msup
                    %mi t
                    %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{t^a\}
            of degree 1, on which the differential acts as
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mrow
                      %mi CE
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi t
                    %mi a
                  %mo ↦
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mfrac
                    %mn 1
                    %mn 2
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi a
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mi c
                  %msup
                    %mi t
                    %mi b
                  %mo ∧
                  %msup
                    %mi t
                    %mi c
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  d_{CE(\mathfrak{g})} : t^a \mapsto - \frac{1}{2} C^a{}_{b c} t^b \wedge t^c
                  \\,.
          %p
            The Weil algebra in turn is generated from these generators
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msup
                    %mi t
                    %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{t^a\}
            in degree 1 and generators
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msup
                    %mi r
                    %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{r^a\}
            in degree 2, with differential given by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi t
                    %mi a
                  %mo ↦
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mfrac
                    %mn 1
                    %mn 2
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi a
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mi c
                  %msup
                    %mi t
                    %mi b
                  %mo ∧
                  %msup
                    %mi t
                    %mi c
                  %mo +
                  %msup
                    %mi r
                    %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  d_{W(\mathfrak{g})} : t^a \mapsto - \frac{1}{2} C^a{}_{b c} t^b \wedge t^c + r^a
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi r
                    %mi a
                  %mo ↦
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi a
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mi c
                  %msup
                    %mi t
                    %mi b
                  %mo ∧
                  %msup
                    %mi r
                    %mi c
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  d_{W(\mathfrak{g})} : r^a \mapsto C^a{}_{b c} t^b \wedge r^c
                  \\,.
          %h3#weil_algebra_of_a_0lie_algebroid Weil algebra of a 0-Lie algebroid
          %p
            A 0-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/truncated"} truncated
            Lie algebroid is one for which the chain complex of modules over the
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi CE
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msubsup
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi A
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝔞
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mrow
                      %mi CE
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝔞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi d
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  CE(\mathfrak{a}) = (\wedge^\bullet_A (\mathfrak{a}^*), d_{CE(\mathfrak{a})})
                  \= (A, d = 0)
                  \\,.
          %p
            For instance for
            = succeed "=" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CartSp"} CartSp
            the theory of
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+algebra"} smooth algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            regarded as an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebroid"} L-∞ algebroid
            is a 0-Lie algebroid with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi CE
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CE(X) = C^\infty(X)
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+algebra"} smooth algebra
            of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+function"} smooth function
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          .num_prop
            %h6#observation_3 Observation
            %p
              The Weil algebra of a 0-Lie algebroid
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K%C3%A4hler+differential"} Kähler
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+complex"} de Rham complex
              of
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo =
                      %mi CE
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A = CE(X)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi dR
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    W(\mathfrak{a}) =
                    (\Omega^\bullet(A), d_{dR})
                    \\,.
          %p
            This Weil algebra is the Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+Lie+algebroid"} tangent Lie algebroid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T X
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+algebra"} de Rham algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^\bullet(X)
            of
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi CE
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi T
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mi dR
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  W(X) = CE(T X) = (\Omega^\bullet(X), d_{dR})
                  \\,.
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Lie+algebra+cohomology"} ∞-Lie algebra cohomology
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebra"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra
            %li
              %p
                %strong Weil algebra
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariant+polynomial"} invariant polynomial
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sullivan+model+of+free+loop+space"} Sullivan model of free loop space
          %h2#references References
          %p Among the original references on Weil algebras for ordinary Lie algebras is
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Henri+Cartan"}> Henri Cartan
              ,
              %em Cohomologie réelle d’un espace fibré principal diffrentielle
              I, II, Séminaire Henri Cartan,
              %p 1949/50, pp. 19-01 – 19-10 and 20-01 – 20-11, CBRM, (1950).
          %p and
          %ul
            %li#Cartan50
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Henri+Cartan"}> Henri Cartan
              ,
              %em Notions d’algébre différentielle; application aux groupes de Lie et aux variétés ou opère un groupe de Lie
              , Colloque de topologie (espaces fibrs), Bruxelles, (1950), pp. 15–27.
          %p
            This also explains the use of the Weil algebra in the calculation of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+cohomology"} equivariant
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+cohomology"} de Rham cohomology
            of manifolds acted on by a compact group. These papers are reprinted, explained and put in a modern context in the book
          %p In monographs:
          %ul
            %li#GHV
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Werner+Greub"}> Werner Greub
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stephen+Halperin"} Stephen Halperin
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ray+Vanstone"} Ray Vanstone
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Connections%2C+Curvature%2C+and+Cohomology"} Connections, Curvature, and Cohomology
              Academic Press (1973)
          %p
            Some remarks on the notation there as compared to ours: our
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_W
            is their
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi δ
                    %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta_W
            on p. 226 (vol III). Their
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi δ
                    %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta_E
            is our
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi CE
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_{CE}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi δ
                    %mi θ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta_\theta
            is our
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mi ρ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_\rho
            (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi θ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta
            \/
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ρ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
            denoting the representation)..
          %p
            In the context of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+de+Rham+cohomology"} equivariant de Rham cohomology
          %ul
            %li#AtiyahBott84
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Atiyah"}> Michael Atiyah
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Raoul+Bott"} Raoul Bott
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The moment map and equivariant cohomology
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0040-9383(84)90021-1"} doi:10.1016/0040-9383(84)90021-1
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.math.stonybrook.edu/~mmovshev/MAT570Spring2008/BOOKS/atiyahbott_moment.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Kalkman93
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jaap+Kalkman"}> Jaap Kalkman
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em BRST model applied to symplectic geometry
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9308132"} arXiv:hep-th/9308132
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://cds.cern.ch/record/568522"} cds:9308132
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.cmp/1104252784"} euclid:1104252784
          %p
            and with an eye towards
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetry
          %ul
            %li#Miettinen96
              %p
                Mauri Miettinen,
                %em Weil Algebras and Supersymmetry
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9612209"}> arXiv:hep-th/9612209
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://cds.cern.ch/record/317377"} cds:317377
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/427720"} spire:427720
            %li#GuilleminSternberg99
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Victor+Guillemin"}> Victor Guillemin
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Shlomo+Sternberg"} Shlomo Sternberg
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Supersymmetry and equivariant de Rham theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-3-662-03992-2"} doi:10.1007/978-3-662-03992-2
          %p
            The (obvious but conceptually important) observation that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra-valued+1-forms"} Lie algebra-valued 1-forms
            regarded as morphisms of graded vector spaces
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ←
                  %msup
                    %mo ∧
                    %mn 1
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo *
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^\bullet(X) \leftarrow \wedge^1 \mathfrak{g}^* : A
            are equivalently morphisms of dg-algebras out of the Weil algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ←
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^\bullet(X) \leftarrow W(\mathfrak{g}) : A
            and that one may think of as the identity
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ←
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi Id
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(\mathfrak{g}) \leftarrow W(\mathfrak{g}) : Id
            as the
            %em
              universal
              = succeed "-connection" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝔤
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            appears in early articles for instance highlighted on p. 15 of
          %ul
            %li
              Franz W. Kamber; Philippe Tondeur,
              %em Semisimplicial Weil algebras and characteristic classes for foliated bundles in Cech cohomology
              , Differential geometry (Proc. Sympos. Pure Math., Vol. XXVII, Stanford Univ., Stanford, Calif., 1973), Part 1, pp. 283–294. Amer. Math. Soc., Providence, R.I., (1975).
          %p A survey of Weil algebras for Lie algebras is also available at
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/eom"}> Encyclopedia of Mathematics
              \:
              %a{:href => "http://eom.springer.de/W/w130050.htm"} Weil algebra of a Lie algebra
          %p
            Weil algebra for
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-infinity+algebra"} L-infinity algebra
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariant+polynomial"} invariant polynomial
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+element"} Chern-Simons element
            = succeed "-Lie" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-Lie+algebra+cohomology"} L-infinity algebra cocycle
            are considered in
          %ul
            %li#SSSI
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"}> Hisham Sati
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jim+Stasheff"} Jim Stasheff
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/L-infinity+algebra+connections"}
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi L
                            %mn ∞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_{\infty}
                    algebra connections and applications to String- and Chern-Simons
                    = succeed "-transport" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              = succeed "," do
                %em Quantum Field Theory
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0801.3480"} arXiv:0801.3480
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-7643-8736-5_17"} doi:10.1007/978-3-7643-8736-5_17
          %p The abstract characterization is due to
          %ul
            %li#FreedHopkins13
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Freed"}> Daniel Freed
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Hopkins"} Michael Hopkins
              = succeed "," do
                %em Chern-Weil forms and abstract homotopy theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1301.5959"} arXiv:1301.5959
          %p
            Further discussion of Weil algebras for the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+Lie+2-algebra"} string Lie 2-algebra
          %ul
            %li#Schmidt19
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lennart+Schmidt"}> Lennart Schmidt
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Twisted Weil Algebras for the String Lie 2-Algebra
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christian+Saemann"} Christian Saemann
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin+Wolf"} Martin Wolf
              (eds.)
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://www.maths.dur.ac.uk/lms/109/index.html"} Higher Structures in M-Theory
              %a{:href => "http://www.maths.dur.ac.uk/lms/"} Durham Symposium
              2018, Fortschritte der Physik 2019 (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1903.02873"}> arXiv:1903.02873
              )
        .revisedby
